{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-1811"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Community Printing Operations"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "1811"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :manufacturing/printing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :environmental-stewardship :local-jobs]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :printing-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies []
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "PrintingOpsAdvisor ⊣ Printing Governor, langgraph-clj StateGraph
 (langgraph.graph, printing.operation/build), append-only audit ledger
 (printing.store/ledger + append-ledger!, MemStore and a DatomicStore
 backed by langchain.db via langchain-store.core). Fixes two prior gaps
 from an earlier attempt at this repo: (1) deferred-stub -- `deps.edn`
 pinned a stale `io.github.com-junkawasaki/langgraph-clj` git/sha
 coordinate to the pre-rename repo, there was no `printing.operation` or
 `printing.phase` namespace at all, and `printing.sim` was a one-line
 `(println ...)` stub that never called the advisor/governor/store, so
 nothing exercised a real StateGraph; (2) fabrication -- `printing.facts`
 held a per-jurisdiction (JPN/USA/GBR) regulatory catalog inventing
 specific statute sections/formal titles (e.g. '労働基準法 §36', 'OSHA
 1910 Subpart Z', 'Product Liability Law §3', '42 USC §7661', 'HSWA
 1974', 'BS ISO 12647-2:2013') nowhere grounded in this repo's own
 README/docs, and `printing.governor`'s equipment-control keyword-block
 list included the literal word 'press', which would hard-block almost
 any printing-domain proposal. Both are removed; `printing.facts` is now
 purely structural (supply-category cost thresholds, press-type
 vocabulary, press/finishing-operation vocabulary, quality-grade
 vocabulary) with zero new regulatory claims beyond this repo's existing
 README/docs prose. Now: a genuinely compiled StateGraph
 (`:intake -> :advise -> :govern -> :decide -+-> :commit / :request-
 approval -> :commit / :hold`) with `interrupt-before
 #{:request-approval}` + in-memory checkpointer for real human-in-the-
 loop resume. A back-office PRINTING OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor for
 press-line management -- not direct press-equipment operation authority
 and not color-certification- or quality-inspection-disposition-
 finalization authority. Six ops (`:log-production-record` /
 `:log-quality-inspection-record` / `:schedule-press-operation` /
 `:flag-quality-concern` / `:order-supplies` / `:release-print-run`), all
 `:effect :propose` only. Eight HARD invariants (press-line-not-
 registered, no-execution, equipment-or-certification-blocked, op-not-
 allowed, production-record-invalid, quality-grade-invalid, print-spec-
 scope-violation, release-without-quality-inspection) plus independent
 cost/quantity/quality-grade/print-spec/confidence verification
 (`printing.registry`) elaborate this blueprint's Governor.
 Quality-concern flagging and print-run release for delivery BOTH ALWAYS
 escalate to a human printer/quality-manager via the compiled graph's
 `:request-approval` node (`interrupt-before`, checkpoint-based resume) --
 matching this repo's own README ('the governor never releases a print
 run for delivery itself'). A print run's `:release-print-run` hard
 checks re-derive its quality-inspection status from `printing.store`'s
 own quality-inspection index (written by a genuinely-committed
 `:log-quality-inspection-record`, never from a release proposal's
 self-report) and its color/print-specification scope from the target
 press line's own `:verified-print-specs` (never from the proposal's own
 claim) -- proven end to end by
 `test/printing/operation_test.cljc`'s `quality-inspection-gates-release`
 exercising commit / hard-hold (unregistered press line, release-
 without-inspection) / escalate-approve / escalate-reject / phase-0-
 forces-escalation through the REAL compiled graph, plus a
 `clojure -M:dev:run` demo runner producing real ledger entries for
 every scenario. MemStore and DatomicStore pass the same store-contract
 test (`test/printing/store_contract_test.cljc`), including the
 quality-inspection index's own upsert semantics. clj-kondo 0 errors,
 demo runnable end-to-end against both Store backends
 (`clojure -M:dev:run`). Governance-doc set and `docs/` were already
 present; CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`, sibling-checkout pattern for
 :local/root deps) and `.gitignore` were missing and are added in this
 fix."}
